  <section>
    <templateId root="1.3.6.1.4.1.19376.1.5.3.1.3.4"/>
    <code code="10164-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="History of Present illness Narrative"/>
    <title>History of Present Illness</title>
    <text><paragraph>Mr. Lincoln returns twelve weeks after starting sertraline 50 mg daily. He says he feels like himself again. He sleeps about seven hours, has kept up his court work and letters, and has added evening walks with a law colleague. His interest in his cases and his friends has returned, and his concentration is back to normal. He has had no side effects since the early nausea and still misses about one dose every two weeks. He has had no suicidal thoughts. The nurse telephone check planned for four weeks after his last visit did not take place. He asks how long he will need to keep taking the medicine. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Element</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Interval change</td><td>Feels like himself; interest and concentration back to normal</td></tr><tr><td>Sleep</td><td>About seven hours a night</td></tr><tr><td>Medication tolerance</td><td>No adverse effects since the early nausea</td></tr><tr><td>Adherence</td><td>Misses about one dose every two weeks</td></tr><tr><td>Safety</td><td>No suicidal thoughts</td></tr><tr><td>PHQ-9</td><td>4, down from 14</td></tr><tr><td>Patient question</td><td>How long to continue sertraline</td></tr></tbody></table></text>

  </section>
</component>

